and I want to highlight a few of them.

535
00:22:33,450 --> 00:22:35,190
And first one is with Polaris,

536
00:22:35,190 --> 00:22:38,970
our student services platform.

537
00:22:38,970 --> 00:22:40,800
We originally designed Polaris

538
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:43,710
to allow a student to get whatever help they want

539
00:22:43,710 --> 00:22:45,480
as quickly as they can get,

540
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,310
and that was kind of the genesis

541
00:22:47,310 --> 00:22:49,740
of our collaboration with Mission College

542
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:52,110
under President Awan's leadership.

543
00:22:52,110 --> 00:22:54,387
President Awan reached out to us about,

544
00:22:54,387 --> 00:22:57,480
and a problem with Mission CARES,

545
00:22:57,480 --> 00:23:01,140
you all know it as College of Desert CARES or Coast CARES,

546
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:04,740
or whatever you are, like with the basic needs,

547
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:06,120
EOPS and others.

548
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:07,770
She wanted to solve the problem

549
00:23:07,770 --> 00:23:10,890
of getting the students the help they need using AI.

550
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:12,483
Let's hear from President Awan.

551
00:23:14,190 --> 00:23:15,570
- [Awan] We have all of our students

552
00:23:15,570 --> 00:23:17,250
complete one application,

553
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:20,430
and we triage those applications and those students

554
00:23:20,430 --> 00:23:23,340
to help them figure out what they qualify for.

555
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:26,460
This process was very, very labor intensive

556
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:29,370
and it was taking up a lot of manpower,

557
00:23:29,370 --> 00:23:32,460
a lot of time auditing spreadsheets

558
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:36,030
and trying to reconcile different systems.

559
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:39,300
And so with reaching out to LightLeap AI,

560
00:23:39,300 --> 00:23:43,110
they were able to help us really start to automate systems,

561
00:23:43,110 --> 00:23:46,563
analyze processes, and use AI and AI agents-

562
00:23:52,683 --> 00:23:55,020
- Well, technical glitch.

563
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:55,853
Without technical glitch,

564
00:23:55,853 --> 00:23:58,307
there is no technical presentation, I guess.

565
00:23:58,307 --> 00:23:59,370
(audience laughs)

566
00:23:59,370 --> 00:24:01,080
The second part is Prism.

567
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,370
We originally started Prism

568
00:24:02,370 --> 00:24:04,560
as a document ingestion platform

569
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:06,000
because Ivy Tech was dealing

570
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:09,300
with hundreds of thousands of transcripts and documents

571
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:10,740
from high school students

572
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:14,310
and they wanted a way to read transcripts

573
00:24:14,310 --> 00:24:15,510
at a speed of light

574
00:24:15,510 --> 00:24:17,640
so that they not only read the transcript,

575
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:19,440
but articulate them quickly.

576
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:22,830
However, we never thought that this technology we created

577
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:26,100
to massively increase online learning

578
00:24:26,100 --> 00:24:29,850
can help with offline learning until I met Clint Cowden.

579
00:24:29,850 --> 00:24:32,970
Clint Cowden, we met at a CSSO conference

580
00:24:32,970 --> 00:24:34,740
while he was eating lunch somewhere,

581
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:37,740
and he presented this unique problem

582
00:24:37,740 --> 00:24:40,590
of connecting AI with offline learning

583
00:24:40,590 --> 00:24:42,330
for his Rising Scholars Program.

584
00:24:42,330 --> 00:24:43,880
Let's hear from Clint directly.

585
00:24:47,550 --> 00:24:51,150
- [Clint] Previous to AI, what we were doing,

586
00:24:51,150 --> 00:24:52,620
especially for something like

587
00:24:52,620 --> 00:24:56,610
when we wanted to get a student accepted to our our college,

588
00:24:56,610 --> 00:25:01,470
we would actually mail them a paper application.

589
00:25:01,470 --> 00:25:06,120
The student would receive that from their pesky,

590
00:25:06,120 --> 00:25:08,970
or a local person at the institution

591
00:25:08,970 --> 00:25:10,380
that would provide them that.

592
00:25:10,380 --> 00:25:13,020
They would fill out that information.

593
00:25:13,020 --> 00:25:16,800
That would then get mailed to Palo Verde College.

594
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:19,140
Really, truth, honestly, Palo Verde College

595
00:25:19,140 --> 00:25:23,610
is very happy to be using LightLeap AI.

596
00:25:23,610 --> 00:25:26,070
It has really helped our college.

597
00:25:26,070 --> 00:25:28,920
So LightLeap AI and Palo Verde College

598
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:32,103
is really excited to continue to move forward.

599
00:25:34,260 --> 00:25:37,080
- So how does all this happen, right?

600
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:40,500
How does the same company that is serving,

601
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:44,790
processing hundreds of gigabytes of data to identify fraud

602
00:25:44,790 --> 00:25:46,950
is also doing document ingestion,

603
00:25:46,950 --> 00:25:49,230
is also doing student services connection?

604
00:25:49,230 --> 00:25:51,330
It's all because of our Atlas platform.

605
00:25:51,330 --> 00:25:54,270
Our Atlas platform is a data modeling system

606
00:25:54,270 --> 00:25:57,240
that can take data from any source

607
00:25:57,240 --> 00:26:00,150
and convert it to actionable intelligence,

608
00:26:00,150 --> 00:26:00,983
and that's one of the things

609
00:26:00,983 --> 00:26:03,810
that we are incredibly excited about.

610
00:26:03,810 --> 00:26:07,680
And all of this is useless if it is just a bunch of scripts

611
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,480
and functions and dashboards.

612
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:10,920
So we tied it all together

613
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:14,310
with a conversational operating system called Ether,

614
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:16,680
which is a chatbot operating system

615
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:19,800
that connects any system, student information system,

616
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:23,460
learning management system, AI agents, or any other systems.

617
00:26:23,460 --> 00:26:28,110
So Gary Moser from Kern came up with this interesting idea

618
00:26:28,110 --> 00:26:31,140
of what if we can connect advisors

619
00:26:31,140 --> 00:26:32,670
to student services needs

620
00:26:32,670 --> 00:26:36,330
so that students can get exactly the right courses

621
00:26:36,330 --> 00:26:38,070
as a result of guided pathways?

622
00:26:38,070 --> 00:26:39,720
So let's hear from Gary directly.

623
00:26:42,540 --> 00:26:45,300
- [Gary] Many of our students have spent time

624
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:46,950
going through and selecting courses

625
00:26:46,950 --> 00:26:49,920
that may not directly apply to the program

626
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:51,480
or degree they're seeking.

627
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:52,950
And we get concerned that the students

628
00:26:52,950 --> 00:26:55,830
are taking an awful long time in the community college

629
00:26:55,830 --> 00:26:57,060
and also taking extra courses

630
00:26:57,060 --> 00:26:59,190
that are not necessarily required,

631
00:26:59,190 --> 00:27:00,750
take that information,

632
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:03,390
and bounce it against their record of program of study

633
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:05,160
and find out where their gaps were,

634
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:07,022
whether they took courses or not,

635
00:27:07,022 --> 00:27:07,920
whether they're missing courses.

636
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:11,400
And then AI would calculate that information

637
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:14,010
and recommend, using N2N as a partner,

638
00:27:14,010 --> 00:27:15,660
we think we can scale this very well,

639
00:27:15,660 --> 00:27:17,130
not only for Banner schools,

640
00:27:17,130 --> 00:27:19,080
but for Colleague schools, PeopleSoft.

641
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:20,400
I don't think it's really gonna matter,

642
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:22,137
because the capability that we have

643
00:27:22,137 --> 00:27:25,560
and partnership that we've built with N2N to be successful

644
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:28,560
is gonna lend itself to years.

645
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:30,270
- I think I'm missing one other platform

646
00:27:30,270 --> 00:27:32,280
we all are familiar with, right?

647
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:33,990
Our fraud elimination platform.

648
00:27:33,990 --> 00:27:35,700
How many of you here are using

649
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:37,503
our fraud elimination platform?

650
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:39,353
Right?

651
00:27:39,353 --> 00:27:42,600
So right now that has been a success story in itself.

652
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,730
When we started this just last year,

653
00:27:44,730 --> 00:27:46,350
speaking of first year birthday,

654
00:27:46,350 --> 00:27:48,930
I was here talking to Futures Summit last year

655
00:27:48,930 --> 00:27:51,810
where we had two districts using the platform

656
00:27:51,810 --> 00:27:54,690
and we processed close to 300,000 applications.

657
00:27:54,690 --> 00:27:58,879
And now, after about a year,

658
00:27:58,879 --> 00:28:02,100
we processed close to three million applications.

659
00:28:02,100 --> 00:28:03,570
And as a result,

660
00:28:03,570 --> 00:28:07,290
we caught close to 850,000 fraudulent factors.

661
00:28:07,290 --> 00:28:09,071
Great round of applause (voice drowned by applause).

662
00:28:09,071 --> 00:28:11,660
(audience applauding)

663
00:28:11,660 --> 00:28:14,430
Speaking of digital area of innovation

664
00:28:14,430 --> 00:28:17,250
or LightLeap innovation or Lightspeed,

665
00:28:17,250 --> 00:28:20,970
in my lifetime of 37 years, that's how old I am,

666
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:22,323
in higher education terms,

667
00:28:23,370 --> 00:28:28,320
I've never seen anything go this fast, not even in general.

668
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:32,021
And it's not just because of one thing,

669
00:28:32,021 --> 00:28:33,573
it's not just because of we have an incredible team

670
00:28:33,573 --> 00:28:35,820
with N2N called LightLeap AI team,

671
00:28:35,820 --> 00:28:38,550
but we also have incredible collaboration

672
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:41,610
with leaders like Jory, Dr. Lambert,

673
00:28:41,610 --> 00:28:45,897
Rupa from Coast, Gary, and Napa Valley, Cerritos,

674
00:28:47,010 --> 00:28:49,410
and every single one of you

675
00:28:49,410 --> 00:28:52,320
deciding to implement fraud detection

676
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:54,420
to solve this systemic problem.

677
00:28:54,420 --> 00:28:56,850
And I'm happy to report that,

678
00:28:56,850 --> 00:28:59,820
I feel that with the incredible collaboration we have,

679
00:28:59,820 --> 00:29:02,400
not just with LightLeap AI team and the Chancellor's Office,

680
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:04,020
but also with the tech center,

681
00:29:04,020 --> 00:29:06,330
I feel that the fraudsters are on retreat,

682
00:29:06,330 --> 00:29:08,220
at least from California.

683
00:29:08,220 --> 00:29:11,190
What we have seen is, with San Bernardino,

684
00:29:11,190 --> 00:29:15,330
there's almost a 30% to 7% drop in fraud.

685
00:29:15,330 --> 00:29:17,100
And some institutions, believe it or not,

686
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:20,130
was dealing with over 74% fraud.

687
00:29:20,130 --> 00:29:22,920
That means that one out of four three applications,

688
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:24,960
three or four applications were fraudulent.

689
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:26,880
And we are able to report

690
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,340
that the fraudsters are on the retreat.

691
00:29:29,340 --> 00:29:31,350
And, again, it's only because

692
00:29:31,350 --> 00:29:33,780
of the incredible collaboration underway

693
00:29:33,780 --> 00:29:36,360
between each of the districts, each of the colleges,

694
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:38,550
and the Chancellor's Office,

695
00:29:38,550 --> 00:29:41,310
and most importantly tech center as well.

696
00:29:41,310 --> 00:29:43,410
And I can go on and on about Orion,

697
00:29:43,410 --> 00:29:45,333
but we don't have that much time.

698
00:29:47,190 --> 00:29:48,840
I wanna end with this slide

699
00:29:48,840 --> 00:29:51,450
