00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:47,760
So we have a special line of speakers for you today,

736
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:50,760
beginning with this morning's fireside chat

737
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:52,560
and our final keynote speaker,

738
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:55,260
Henk Rogers of Tetris, acclaimed,

739
00:31:55,260 --> 00:31:57,240
and physical visionary philanthropist

740
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:59,223
of the Blue Planet Alliance.

741
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,650
As we gather here this morning,

742
00:32:01,650 --> 00:32:04,050
we're not just talking about the future.

743
00:32:04,050 --> 00:32:05,310
As Chancellor Christian mentioned,

744
00:32:05,310 --> 00:32:08,220
we're actively creating it.

745
00:32:08,220 --> 00:32:11,670
Vision 2030 is our roadmap for this journey.

746
00:32:11,670 --> 00:32:14,730
Centering equity, climate action,

747
00:32:14,730 --> 00:32:18,990
and the transformative potential of artificial intelligence

748
00:32:18,990 --> 00:32:20,703
in all the work that we do.

749
00:32:21,990 --> 00:32:23,973
This isn't just policy on paper,

750
00:32:24,870 --> 00:32:29,520
it's our commitment to 2.1 million students

751
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:31,440
who walk through our doors,

752
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:36,210
trusting us to prepare them for a world that's changing

753
00:32:36,210 --> 00:32:38,313
at unprecedented speed.

754
00:32:39,990 --> 00:32:42,060
And while these imperatives require us

755
00:32:42,060 --> 00:32:44,970
to harness technological innovation,

756
00:32:44,970 --> 00:32:48,993
we must do so with unwavering commitment to justice.

757
00:32:50,190 --> 00:32:53,640
Our Board of Governors has given us a clear mandate

758
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,740
to address these challenges

759
00:32:55,740 --> 00:32:58,203
on behalf of the citizens of California.

760
00:33:00,150 --> 00:33:04,320
As we stand at the crossroads of technological advancement,

761
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:07,020
we must examine artificial intelligence

762
00:33:07,020 --> 00:33:09,120
through an intersectional lens

763
00:33:09,120 --> 00:33:12,370
that considers both its extraordinary potential

764
00:33:13,320 --> 00:33:14,913
and its profound risk.

765
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:20,550
AI offers unprecedented opportunities

766
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:23,910
to close equity and opportunity gaps,

767
00:33:23,910 --> 00:33:26,580
yet we cannot ignore its potential

768
00:33:26,580 --> 00:33:30,420
for devastating socioeconomic impacts

769
00:33:30,420 --> 00:33:35,250
on local communities, women and the families they care for,

770
00:33:35,250 --> 00:33:36,333
and the Global South,

771
00:33:37,350 --> 00:33:40,020
particularly as the race for natural resources

772
00:33:40,020 --> 00:33:44,280
to fuel AI infrastructure accelerates climate change

773
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,680
and further marginalizes vulnerable populations.

774
00:33:48,750 --> 00:33:50,490
California's Community Colleges

775
00:33:50,490 --> 00:33:52,890
have the unique power and responsibility

776
00:33:52,890 --> 00:33:57,513
to tackle the state's and nation's greatest challenges.

777
00:33:58,440 --> 00:34:01,320
And as the nation's largest higher education system,

778
00:34:01,320 --> 00:34:05,040
we are positioned to drive equitable solutions

779
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:09,060
precisely because of the diversity of our students

780
00:34:09,060 --> 00:34:14,060
and our staff who reflect the larger global community,

781
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:15,900
giving us the insights

782
00:34:15,900 --> 00:34:18,873
that other institutions simply cannot match.

783
00:34:20,430 --> 00:34:23,040
So today, we have the honor

784
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:25,710
of hearing from two pioneering women

785
00:34:25,710 --> 00:34:27,900
whose scholarship and leadership

786
00:34:27,900 --> 00:34:32,640
are reshaping how we understand technology, power,

787
00:34:32,640 --> 00:34:34,473
and justice in education.

788
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:38,430
Their voices are essential

789
00:34:38,430 --> 00:34:40,740
as we work to build more equitable futures

790
00:34:40,740 --> 00:34:42,390
for our students and communities.

791
00:34:43,500 --> 00:34:46,710
Returning to Futures Summit 2025,

792
00:34:46,710 --> 00:34:49,800
