The accumulation of all of our personal data

1050
00:47:10,290 --> 00:47:13,290
that was then used to train these AI models,

1051
00:47:13,290 --> 00:47:15,750
it could not exist without the fact

1052
00:47:15,750 --> 00:47:18,120
that we have sort of been lulled

1053
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:22,290
into this sense that technology just,

1054
00:47:22,290 --> 00:47:24,450
we just have to lay down and accept it.

1055
00:47:24,450 --> 00:47:28,980
Like, we just have to, if we don't use these tools,

1056
00:47:28,980 --> 00:47:33,180
then we're going to somehow get lost in this future

1057
00:47:33,180 --> 00:47:35,070
and be ill-prepared.

1058
00:47:35,070 --> 00:47:37,470
And so that's what I ultimately wanted

1059
00:47:37,470 --> 00:47:39,420
to explore in the book, is to show that,

1060
00:47:39,420 --> 00:47:41,940
like, this is the same thing.

1061
00:47:41,940 --> 00:47:43,650
We've seen this story before.

1062
00:47:43,650 --> 00:47:46,170
We've seen Altman as a character before.

1063
00:47:46,170 --> 00:47:49,680
And even though OpenAI talks about it being a nonprofit,

1064
00:47:49,680 --> 00:47:52,290
